{"title":"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> for which there exists a positive real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed03d4045f13580853bc7c804d90838ddbdde71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=x\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be irrational because the product of a rational number and an irrational number is irrational (but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer). Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is rational.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524a8f998ea0ee544cfb2c6f086b045fa00296f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a + \\frac{b}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"76\" height=\"37\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are nonnegative integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1536ad6dd1922ffa135f9942eeda97cc469cab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le b &lt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> (essentially, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a mixed number). Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608014af5acedd422d897ce289b199abf4e27fb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\left(a + \\frac{b}{c}\\right) \\left\\lfloor a +\\frac{b}{c} \\right\\rfloor \\Rightarrow n = \\left(a + \\frac{b}{c}\\right)a = a^2 + \\frac{ab}{c}\\]\" width=\"400\" height=\"43\" /> \n</p><p>Here it is sufficient for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929b96e76b59eda5196511f84ccd6adcedab8763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"37\" /> to be an integer. We can use casework to find values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> based on the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea723f87961b337f21bbd4b2684cc89b9b1a2c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0 \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> nothing because n is positive\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b596300114baa8c176d69e47ad08aa2ccc9eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1 \\implies \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{0}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a62cf033a972f80e791fb79511332257dbf96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2 \\implies \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{0}{2},\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1abf708a6635cdee04f4046006306345a5f5b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3 \\implies\\frac{b}{c} =\\frac{0}{3},\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe pattern continues up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c30925075c98bcb628589aae8a73db5bdbe25faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e07a77fbd1dfd66033443e1917e56cc7cd142b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 32$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7607e5b388efd688f39364400b9b367b52d5067f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. However if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c30925075c98bcb628589aae8a73db5bdbe25faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, the largest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95dffea3975c87a4b98406acf4a9f256320b7774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 + \\frac{30}{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is still less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore the number of positive integers for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16a117c2d7015a54b3bfe37b0605a6bc67e187a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+...+31 = \\frac{31 \\cdot 32}{2} = \\boxed{496}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"297\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21debf1ddc14dabebadacf8e745e89022d9bf997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" /> is continuous over the region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c4977b1c4584625cbaecd49b1486374b677cbc06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in [k, k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, it takes all values in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa4197adac1e49f890afc8d322698dd9195f7ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[k\\lfloor k\\rfloor, (k+1)\\lfloor k+1\\rfloor) = [k^2, (k+1)k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"299\" height=\"21\" /> over that interval. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572ee88257b43d5cd70e371a18964b3c87860a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;32$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb259d4ff87c723a75bb3e9a13e3cfbba9b3b9ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 &gt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737bf9b9ddaf4d4879ecdb1dbf30e8080954c19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, the maximum value attained is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bfc079b1a8f858484784cccc0f2364048fe5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31*32 &lt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />. It follows that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d46cbbde6f602e70d870fa8efcf811b67fb462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{31} (k+1)k-k^2  = \\sum_{k=1}^{31} k = \\frac{31\\cdot 32}{2} = \\boxed{496}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"338\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Bounding gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba3e404a5c0f6abe914687ed92841a0565c3411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\le n&lt;x^2+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"130\" height=\"19\" />. Thus there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, for each value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. Checking, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b0e691dbf186b4b731d15c536b9420596b1f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31^2+31=992&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fcad0aa75a3eaa7048536e761eabba553f9a4e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+2+3+...+31= \\boxed{496}\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"23\" /> such values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Here writer's x and question's x are different.<br />\nHere writer means [x] everywhere he writes x<br />\nso you can let [x] = k and then use the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/0/7c0099b4ddaa8b0f7fd0367c655e6740400d0e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2\\le n&lt;k^2+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />.<br />\nthis inequality comes from [x] = k<br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130efa8e88758a78f3da02ed7c7eb903e4c426b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\le x&lt;k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbebe86b8066f5a6d3a10a091e33b8c7df50054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k[x]\\le x[x]&lt;(k+1)[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" /><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c6a2570776b599af470055799551d1322d7d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2\\le n&lt;(k+1)k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" /><br /> further you can proceed.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>After a bit of experimenting, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934b6be3c265c2b0da8ee3a02d27a9e80327e9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=l^2+s, s &lt; 2n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />. We claim that I (the integer part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />) = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> . (Prove it yourself using contradiction&#160;!) so now we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1447205614978a5dd72514ee0233b86ea02d6566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=l+\\frac{s}{l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"33\" />. This implies that solutions exist iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d950ba9b1003dfa308cf618b98511c4a7e2924a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;l$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, or for all natural numbers of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806756e23140eb58806a2c1d60389c35ba4db1f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2+s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d950ba9b1003dfa308cf618b98511c4a7e2924a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;l$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. \nHence, 1 solution exists for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7d802f36cb7350777c714781c597141d2d6796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />! 2 for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6fbb515c22e2b4d5f4b9a2b164b626a4e3e2a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l=2$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> and so on. Therefore our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe86bd988c6263a68b3d8274362a0150e8a6ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31+30+\\dots+1= \\boxed{496}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Notice we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9975046a75bf5468d4d388a619032b73064513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - \\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. \nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0d0750fd15dd7f55fbe467c8a272528a450c18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\leq x(x - \\{x\\}) \\leq 999.\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We now have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649cee62e4e3afa88b41735fd58e325c5faf8073.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\leq x^{2} - x\\{x\\} \\leq 999.\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b125f43db7d1ed5a0fcc9a27ab82364d1f2a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> ranges from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we can rewrite as \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0e7878ff426c5e6c64276c327f373cb445fb91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\leq x^{2} \\leq 999 + x.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Notice all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy this inequality range from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Now every range from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f801b9f0ef3c2c1d614cd42c8abd34ebedf7c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> results in exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> solutions that give a positive integer solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \nThe first range is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the last range is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, by using our above lemma, we can find the total number of solutions:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f19c049895ab126ee83887aad0deb2a50bb19e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+2+\\cdots+31 = \\frac{31 \\cdot 32}{2} = \\boxed{496}.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5beeaccac77b6ae914ba67cede58b36af373ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a + \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7e5c06a1082a671eec46cd0eb16cffc68e70afe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq \\alpha &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />. Then we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d0810622a7d9c916f3503810cef20028016f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + \\alpha)(a) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad6c989fb096c538361a22a127f1a6e1760b036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor a + \\alpha \\rfloor = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Now we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/5192612556422d0f97926dbda7d7e9347951c96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a \\alpha = n \\implies \\alpha = \\frac{n - a^2}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"237\" height=\"41\" /> so we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f4651e1e5016c96045eeefae2540c00a620bcb79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq \\frac{n - a^2}{a} &lt; 1 \\implies a^2 \\leq n &lt; a^2 + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"298\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, it means all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> possible are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c8d2e84d97c9e3d130634d862ef24a8cb715d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> inclusive. The number of possibilities here is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/2619251e64c9f8f597789b425c70eba2d559fe71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a - 1 - a^2 + 1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de87a38aa7b2c7b68a8fb7ec6a311c219bce70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8d1aa569748eb902571b98522ab7ad85f45979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 &lt; 1000 \\implies a \\leq 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"181\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3c09211dff69f0f1af27d502459ebf8afc557c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a \\leq 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. In other words, we simply have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d889e6fcb875ec40eac01454c72c963a1734e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\cdots + 31 = \\boxed{496}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"189\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GqiNJuOsl1w?si=yd68PahrwevAa6fn\">2012 AIME II #10</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 6</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II\" title=\"2012 AIME II\">2012 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041013\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 611/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18764/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.096      1 -total\n 59.85%    7.838      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.55%    5.049      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10907:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017041013 and revision id 283612. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}